p.src:
The interview then widens from selling to the difference between being rich and being wealthy. Zane defines rich as making roughly $\$4\mathrm{M}$ to $\$10\mathrm{M}$ per year. He reserves wealthy for billionaire-level assets that are deployed and working: $\begin{aligned}
\text{rich} &\sim \$4\mathrm{M}\text{--}\$10\mathrm{M}\ \text{per year},\\
\text{wealthy} &\sim \$1\mathrm{B}\ \text{in deployed assets}.\end{aligned}$

